  "knowledge": [
    {
      "id": "kb-hooks",
      "title": "Hooks: win the first 2 seconds",
      "tags": [
        "viral",
        "hook"
      ],
      "body": "People decide to stay or scroll in about 1 second. Every episode must open with a HOOK shot.\n\n**Rules**\n- Text on screen from frame 1 (big, 4–8 words). Never start on a blank or slow fade.\n- First spoken word within 0.5–0.8s.\n- Open a loop: a question the viewer needs answered.\n- Start in the middle of the action or with the twist, then rewind (\"3 saal pehle…\").\n\n**Hook formulas that work for love-story series**\n1. Flash-forward: \"Aaj hum shaadi kar rahe hain… par shuruaat ek WiFi hotspot se hui thi.\"\n2. Mystery object: \"Ek password-less hotspot ne meri zindagi badal di.\"\n3. POV: \"POV: tumhara future husband tumhara hotspot use kar raha hai 😭\"\n4. Contradiction: \"Mujhe engineering nahi karni thi… aur wahi meri love story ban gayi.\"\n5. Direct question: \"Kya ek stranger ka friend request accept karna chahiye?\"\n6. Countdown: \"Strangers se forever tak: Part 3.\"\n7. Callback: \"Pichle part mein hotspot connect hua tha… aaj kuch aur connect hua.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-retention",
      "title": "Retention: keep them till the end",
      "tags": [
        "viral",
        "editing"
      ],
      "body": "- Length: 20–45s per episode (sweet spot about 30s).\n- Change the visual every 2–5s (new shot, zoom or camera move). No shot longer than 6.5s.\n- Subtitles always on (most people watch muted). Big, high-contrast, inside the safe zone.\n- Mix narration with character dialogue; real voices and emotions keep attention.\n- Music: mood shifts per scene, ducked under voices; a sting or rise right before the cliffhanger.\n- End on a cliffhanger plus \"Next: Ep N\". Never resolve the question in the same episode.\n- Make the ending loop: the last frame should make sense going back into the first (boosts replays)."
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-series",
      "title": "Series strategy",
      "tags": [
        "viral",
        "growth"
      ],
      "body": "- Post as numbered parts (\"Part 1\", \"Ep 1\") so people binge and follow.\n- Pin Part 1 to the top of the profile; create an Instagram highlight or YouTube playlist \"Strangers to Forever\".\n- Post consistently: same time, every 1–2 days while the series is running.\n- Reply to comments with the next part's teaser; ask viewers to guess what happens.\n- Repost the best moment as a standalone teaser reel (\"the hotspot moment\")."
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-captions",
      "title": "Captions & hashtags",
      "tags": [
        "viral",
        "publish"
      ],
      "body": "**Caption formula:** Hook line + 1 line of context + question/CTA + \"Follow for Part N\".\nExample: \"He connected to my hotspot before he connected to my heart 📶❤️ Would YOU accept a stranger's request? 👇 Follow for Part 2\"\n\n**Hashtags (5–12):** mix big plus niche.\n- Big: #lovestory #reels #trending #couplegoals\n- Niche: #engineeringlove #collegelovestory #bangalorelove #strangerstolovers #animatedstory #hinglishstory\n- Series tag: #StrangersToForever"
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-timing",
      "title": "Posting times (India)",
      "tags": [
        "publish"
      ],
      "body": "- Best windows: 7–9 PM IST (prime), 12–2 PM IST (lunch), 9–11 PM on weekends.\n- YouTube Shorts: same reel, add #Shorts and a searchable title.\n- Instagram: share to feed ON, add the series cover, use a trending audio at low volume only if it doesn't fight the voices."
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-style",
      "title": "Style guide",
      "tags": [
        "production"
      ],
      "body": "- 1080×1920, 30fps. Keep text inside the safe zone: away from the top 250px and the bottom 420px (Instagram UI).\n- Colour code: pink = Ishita's world, blue = Vihaan's world, purple = when they're together.\n- Title banner: navy box, \"Strangers to Forever\", \"Forever\" in gold, with the episode tag.\n- Language: Hinglish (Devanagari for Hindi, English words in English).\n- Voice tags for eleven_v3: [softly], [warmly], [whispers], [sad], [cheerful], [firmly], [laughs], [pause]."
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-cast",
      "title": "Voice cast",
      "tags": [
        "production",
        "voice"
      ],
      "body": "- Narrator: Yatin (Sacred & Divine Love Storyteller). Warm, soothing male storyteller.\n- Ishita: Tarini (Calm and Measured).\n- Vihaan: Amit Gupta (Lover Boy Romantic).\n- Zoya: Monika Sogam (Friendly and Reassuring).\n- Appa: Shardul K (deep, authoritative).\n- Amma, Tanvi: cast when they first speak."
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-privacy",
      "title": "Privacy rules",
      "tags": [
        "privacy"
      ],
      "body": "- Never use real names of people, the real hometown, or the real college. Real ↔ series names live only in the private name map (Settings → Privacy), never committed to git.\n- Story dumps are auto-anonymized when saved.\n- Every episode is leak-scanned before publishing; publishing is blocked if a real name is found.\n- Avoid identifiable details: exact train numbers, real college logos, faces of real people."
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-workflow",
      "title": "Production workflow",
      "tags": [
        "production"
      ],
      "body": "1. Dump the story in **Story Inbox** (any language, as messy as you like).\n2. Click **Ask Claude**, then tell Claude Code \"check the studio\". Claude writes the episode (hook, shots, Hinglish lines, moods, caption).\n3. Review in **Episode Editor**: tweak lines, emotions, moods.\n4. **Generate voices** (ElevenLabs), then **Generate score**.\n5. Check the **Viral Score**; fix anything red.\n6. **Render**, preview, and **Publish** or schedule (YouTube and Instagram direct; export pack for the rest)."
    }
  ],
